    {
      "id": "p4wskmi",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Metals are malleable, ductile, lustrous, and good conductors of heat and electricity.",
        "Non-metals are generally brittle, non-lustrous, and poor conductors of heat and electricity.",
        "Metals form basic or amphoteric oxides when reacted with oxygen, whereas non-metals form acidic or neutral oxides.",
        "The reactivity series ranks metals in decreasing order of their chemical reactivity, dictating displacement reactions.",
        "Extraction techniques depend on reactivity: highly reactive metals are extracted by electrolysis, while moderately reactive metals undergo calcination or roasting followed by reduction."
      ],
      "id": "5epmfgg"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qt7te3w",
      "content": "• Metals are elements that are generally hard, shiny and good conductors of heat and electricity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7m17eos",
      "content": "• They are usually solid at room temperature (except mercury)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rzs55yd",
      "content": "• Examples: Iron, Copper, Aluminium, Gold, Silver."
    },
    {
      "id": "a23nu4w",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Physical Properties of Metals"
    },
    {
