      "content": "8. Extraction of Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Mercury is the only metal that is liquid at room temperature, while Bromine is the only liquid non-metal.",
        "Sodium and Potassium are exceptionally soft metals that can be cut with a knife and are stored in kerosene to prevent reaction with moisture and air.",
        "Aluminium Oxide (Al2O3) and Zinc Oxide (ZnO) are amphoteric oxides because they react with both acids and bases to produce salt and water.",
        "Aqua Regia is a freshly prepared mixture of concentrated Hydrochloric Acid and concentrated Nitric Acid in a 3:1 ratio, capable of dissolving gold and platinum."
      ],
      "id": "k4wmccs"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4j87y2z",
      "content": "• Highly reactive metals are extracted by electrolysis."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lvf9w3t",
      "content": "• Moderately reactive metals are extracted by reduction using carbon."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2nmopu2",
      "content": "• Less reactive metals are often found in free state."
    },
    {
      "id": "gch36rq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k43e7mm",
      "content": "• Metals are good conductors of heat and electricity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fdt1tzd",
      "content": "• Non-metals are generally poor conductors."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d66ra7e",
      "content": "• Mercury is the only metal that is liquid at room temperature."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kbbtq91",
